<title>FRANCE: EU scraps wheat, flour export taxes. [CORRECTED 18:40 GMT]</title>
<headline>EU scraps wheat, flour export taxes. [CORRECTED 18:40 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union on Thursday scrapped export taxes for all types of wheat and flour and replaced them with an entry known as &quot;nil value,&quot; European Commission officials said.</p>
<p>(Corrects by inserting words &quot;..and replaced them with an entry known as &quot;nil value,&quot;... ).</p>
<p>EU member country officials had said earlier the taxes had been brought down to zero from previous levels that included five Ecus per tonne for the main category of soft wheat.</p>
<p>The difference is vital because &quot;nil value&quot; licences are valid for just 30 days instead of the normal four to five months and their value cannot be fixed in advance, meaning it can be altered by the Commission before the licences are used.</p>
</text>
